.TH tensor-wasm-serve 1  "tensor-wasm-serve "
.SH NAME
tensor\-wasm\-serve \- Run the TensorWasm HTTP API gateway in\-process (binds and serves)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtensor\-wasm\-serve\fR [\fB\-\-addr\fR] [\fB\-\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-tenant\-header\-policy\fR] [\fB\-\-cors\-origin\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-body\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the TensorWasm HTTP API gateway in\-process (binds and serves).

Stands up the axum router from \fBtensor\-wasm\-api\fR's \fBbuild_router_with_full_config\fR,
binds it to \fB\-\-addr\fR, and serves until Ctrl\-C. Flags map onto the existing
API config surface; knobs not yet exposed by the api crate fall back to the
\fBTENSOR_WASM_API_*\fR environment variables documented in
\fBcrates/tensor-wasm-api/src/lib.rs\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-addr\fR \fI<ADDR>\fR [default: 127.0.0.1:8080]
Address to bind the HTTP server to (e.g. \fB127.0.0.1:8080\fR, \fB0.0.0.0:8080\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<TOKEN>\fR
Bearer token accepted by the gateway. Repeat to allowlist multiple tokens.
If omitted, the gateway reads \fBTENSOR_WASM_API_TOKENS\fR from the environment;
empty/unset there enables dev\-mode pass\-through with a startup warning.
.TP
\fB\-\-tenant\-header\-policy\fR \fI<POLICY>\fR [default: optional]
Policy for the \fBX\-TensorWasm\-Tenant\fR header. \fBoptional\fR mirrors
\fBTENSOR_WASM_API_REQUIRE_TENANT\fR unset; \fBrequired\fR mirrors
\fBTENSOR_WASM_API_REQUIRE_TENANT=1\fR. Possible values: \fBoptional\fR, \fBrequired\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-cors\-origin\fR \fI<ORIGIN>\fR
Origin to allow via CORS. Repeat for multiple origins. Currently
informational \(em the api crate does not yet expose a programmatic
\fBCorsConfig\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-body\-bytes\fR \fI<BYTES>\fR [default: 67108864]
Maximum inbound request body size, in bytes. Currently informational;
the gateway uses its compiled\-in 64 MiB cap until \fBtensor\-wasm\-api\fR
exposes a programmatic body\-cap knob.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBTENSOR_WASM_API_TOKENS\fR
Fallback bearer\-token allowlist when \fB\-\-token\fR is not supplied; see
\fBcrates/tensor-wasm-api/src/middleware.rs\fR.
.TP
\fBTENSOR_WASM_API_REQUIRE_TENANT\fR
Set to \fB1\fR to require the \fBX\-TensorWasm\-Tenant\fR header (overrides
the default \fBoptional\fR policy when \fB\-\-tenant\-header\-policy\fR is omitted).
.TP
\fBTENSOR_WASM_API_RATE_LIMIT_QPS\fR, \fBTENSOR_WASM_API_RATE_LIMIT_BURST\fR
Per\-token rate limiter knobs; zero or unset disables the limiter.
.TP
\fBTENSOR_WASM_API_AUDIT_LOG\fR
Selects the audit\-log sink (defaults to stdout).
.SH SEE ALSO
tensor\-wasm(1), tensor\-wasm\-deploy(1), tensor\-wasm\-invoke(1), tensor\-wasm\-metrics(1)
